  "raw": {
    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/graduate-associate-dean-school-of-nursing-f00630-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630",
      "description": "Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 - New York, United States Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 - New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 New York, United States Faculty Full-time $115,000 - $160,000 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner (NP) with academic leadership experience who can simultaneously steward program quality, contribute to the development of new programs, cultivate meaningful clinical and academic partnerships, and contribute to the School’s strategic direction. KEY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: Faculty and Academic Administration • Supervise program directors, specialty leads, and other academic administrative roles within the graduate programs. • Consult with Program Directors regarding faculty performance in academic affairs. • Advance graduate program planning and implementation by providing program-specific leadership and by engaging faculty and program leaders. • Develop and implement graduate program-specific policies and procedures in collaboration with faculty and program leaders, ensuring they are consistent with school-wide academic operations policies, procedures, and processes coordinated through the Associate Dean for Academic Operations. • Provide leadership for graduate nursing curriculum and student academic oversight, including curriculum quality, student progression, academic standards, program-specific student concerns, and licensure and certification pass rates, in collaboration with faculty, program leaders, and the Senior Associate Dean to ensure alignment with school-wide academic policies and operational processes. • Support the successful operation of new programs, and committees within the School. Curriculum • Lead the development of new graduate programs that meet workforce needs • Assist in the design, development, evaluation, and continuous improvement of nursing curricula to ensure alignment with accreditation standards, licensure requirements, and emerging trends in healthcare education. • Collaborate with faculty and program directors to integrate evidence-based practice, health equity, technology, and innovation across all academic programs. • Assist in leading curriculum review processes, including course mapping, assessment planning, and outcome evaluation to support academic rigor and student success. • Oversee the implementation of academic policies and procedures related to curriculum, progression, grading, and program integrity within the graduate programs. Assessment: • Oversee the School’s ongoing assessment process for graduate programs, including timely submission of required reports. • Work with Program Directors to ensure syllabi clearly articulate student learning and professional development outcomes • Ensure that student learning outcomes are achieved and measurable through both qualitative and quantitative methods. • Promote data-informed assessment of student academic achievement and retention. • Partner with the Dean and Sr. Associate Dean to implement and evaluate the school’s institutional effectiveness plan. • Assist the CNO with the timely preparation and submission of reports related to curriculum for internal governance, accreditation bodies, and regulatory agencies. Teaching: • Teach a minimum of 12 credits annually to remain actively engaged in teaching excellence, maintain familiarity with the learning management system, and understand evolving instructional practices and student needs. Other Responsibilities: • Serve on a twelve-month contract. • Perform additional duties as assigned by School Dean. Education and Experience Requirements: • Possess a doctorate degree (DNP, or PhD) in nursing or a related field with a graduate degree in nursing • Minimum of seven years of teaching experience at postsecondary level. • Demonstrate eligibility for and maintenance of unrestricted licensure in New York State as a Registered Nurse (RN) and as a nurse practitioner is required. • Eligibility for rank of Associate or Full Professor required. • Five years of progressive administrative experience Skills and Competencies: • Deep familiarity with graduate nursing education across multiple program types, including clinical masters and doctorate programs, and an understanding of the distinct needs of each. • Ability to synthesize conceptual frameworks into teaching applications, using current and best practices in instruction, including online modalities. • Experience navigating accreditation processes and regulatory requirements. • Demonstrate capacity to manage multiple projects, set priorities, and coordinate efforts within and across academic units. • The ability to analyze enrollment trends, workforce demands, and licensure and certification outcomes and translate findings into strategic, actionable plans. • Strong written and verbal communication skills; effective in both face-to-face and virtual environments. • Demonstrated interpersonal and collaborative skills in working with faculty, students, staff, and external stakeholders. • Knowledge of and/or experience with distance education models is preferred. • Commitment to fostering a positive, team-oriented environment that reflects respect, equity, and professional integrity. • A scholarly profile that supports meaningful contribution to national conversations on graduate nursing education and workforce development. Physical/Other Requirements: • Must be able to perform tasks that may involve pushing, pulling, moving, or lifting up to 50 lbs., with reasonable accommodations as needed. • Must meet all role-specific general health and safety requirements in accordance with university policies and guidelines upon hire, with reasonable accommodations provided as needed. Apply Now First Name (required) 75c686de Last Name (required) 7739a3ab Email (required) bb4115aa Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert b74fd568 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Nursing School of Nursing Locations New York, United States New York, United States First Name (required) 201757f2 Last Name (required) a19da71f Email (required) 4f26118f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner (NP) with academic leadership experience who can simultaneously steward program quality, contribute to the development of new programs, cultivate meaningful clinical and academic partnerships, and contribute to the School’s strategic direction. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00559) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This position is for the undergraduate programs that run on weekdays and weekends on the Dobbs Ferry (Westchester) and Bronx campuses. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00597) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This position is for the undergraduate programs that run on weekdays and weekends on the Dobbs Ferry (Westchester) and Bronx campuses. About Mercy Mercy University is a dynamic, independent, coeducational New York City area university that offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate degree and certificate programs in six schools: Business, Education, Health and Natural Sciences, Liberal Arts, Nursing, and Social and Behavioral Sciences. Mercy is the region's largest private, nonprofit, Minority-Serving Institution, proud to serve a student body that is highly diverse. As a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI), Mercy University, has been ranked nationally among top colleges in the country for Hispanics by the Hispanic Association of Colleges and Universities (HACU) and by Excelencia in Education, earning their prestigious Seal of Excelencia for intentionally serving Latino students. Mercy University was further recognized by HACU as a national leader in awarding bachelor's degrees to Hispanics in several disciplines, including Psychology, Sociology, and Business. Westchester Magazine has also named Mercy the Best College in Westchester County in 2019, 2020, and 2022. Mercy is committed to offering an inclusive learning environment to help a diverse student body set a course for their future. To support its student body, Mercy has been awarded a number of federal grants which enable us to better develop and deliver education to our students. Mercy’s student body reflects the rich diversity of the New York metropolitan area. Enrollment, including full-time and part-time undergraduates and graduates, is approximately 8,800. Mercy students learn on campuses in Dobbs Ferry, the Bronx, and Manhattan as well as online. At Mercy University we strive to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. Our Mission: Mercy University is committed to providing motivated students the opportunity to transform their lives through higher education by offering liberal arts and professional programs in personalized and high-quality learning environments, thus preparing students to embark on rewarding careers, to continue learning throughout their lives and to act ethically and responsibly in a changing world. Benefits Eligible: Mercy University strives to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. EEO Statement Mercy University is an equal opportunity employer. Mercy University actively engages in recruiting a diverse workforce and student body that includes members of historically underrepresented groups and strives to build and sustain a welcoming and supportive campus community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, pregnancy, height, weight, genetic information, disability, or protected veteran status. As part of this commitment, Mercy University will ensure that persons with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations for the hiring process. If reasonable accommodation is needed, please contact The Office of Human Resources at (914) 674-7839, Option 6 or via email at HR@mercy.edu. The posted salary range for this position is based on several legitimate, non-discriminatory factors set by the organization. Mercy is committed to ensuring equal pay opportunities for equal work regardless of gender, race, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local pay equity laws. Campus Safety Mercy University is committed to providing a safe and welcoming environment for all. Information regarding campus safety can be found here . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
