    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/studio-administrator-pt-n00118-dobbs-ferry-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Studio Administrator (PT)- N00118",
      "description": "Studio Administrator (PT)- N00118 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Studio Administrator (PT)- N00118 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Studio Administrator (PT)- N00118 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Part-Time $20.00 per hour Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Assistant Studio Manager assists the Studio Manager with program needs and prepares the facilities for courses and all program activities. In addition, the Assistant Studio Manager provides daily technical assistance to students and faculty including weekly training workshops as needed. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Manage Music Facilities on Nights/ Weekends Assist Studio Manager with Managing and coordinating studio operations, student staff, facilities scheduling, security and monitoring of the program’s labs and studios including the development of associated policies, procedures, training manuals and regular communication with program constituents Assist Studio Manager with Managing technical design, upgrades, updates, purchasing, installation and maintenance, of equipment in studios & labs. Manage the organization, storage, and records of all inventory of equipment and supplies for the program’s studios and labs Provide tours and information for prospective students as needed Provide technical services for campus concerts Daily scheduling of studio access Daily technical assistance to students Daily preparation of labs and studios, maintenance and equipment set-up Frequent troubleshooting of technical problems in studios and labs Weekly studio and lab hardware and software maintenance Update inventory database as needed Required Skills & Experience: Three years of music and audio software operation experience Three years of recording studio operation experience One year Audio system design and installation experience Education Requirements: Bachelor's degree in music technology or related field required Apply Now First Name (required) f1748cbc Last Name (required) 9b8687c5 Email (required) cee280df Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert a1d92af6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost's Office Provost's Office Locations Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) a2c1b971 Last Name (required) 91e3a1d1 Email (required) ab3c3ace Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner (NP) with academic leadership experience who can simultaneously steward program quality, contribute to the development of new programs, cultivate meaningful clinical and academic partnerships, and contribute to the School’s strategic direction. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00559) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This position is for the undergraduate programs that run on weekdays and weekends on the Dobbs Ferry (Westchester) and Bronx campuses. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00597) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This position is for the undergraduate programs that run on weekdays and weekends on the Dobbs Ferry (Westchester) and Bronx campuses. About Mercy Mercy University is a dynamic, independent, coeducational New York City area university that offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate degree and certificate programs in six schools: Business, Education, Health and Natural Sciences, Liberal Arts, Nursing, and Social and Behavioral Sciences. Mercy is the region's largest private, nonprofit, Minority-Serving Institution, proud to serve a student body that is highly diverse. As a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI), Mercy University, has been ranked nationally among top colleges in the country for Hispanics by the Hispanic Association of Colleges and Universities (HACU) and by Excelencia in Education, earning their prestigious Seal of Excelencia for intentionally serving Latino students. Mercy University was further recognized by HACU as a national leader in awarding bachelor's degrees to Hispanics in several disciplines, including Psychology, Sociology, and Business. Westchester Magazine has also named Mercy the Best College in Westchester County in 2019, 2020, and 2022. Mercy is committed to offering an inclusive learning environment to help a diverse student body set a course for their future. To support its student body, Mercy has been awarded a number of federal grants which enable us to better develop and deliver education to our students. Mercy’s student body reflects the rich diversity of the New York metropolitan area. Enrollment, including full-time and part-time undergraduates and graduates, is approximately 8,800. Mercy students learn on campuses in Dobbs Ferry, the Bronx, and Manhattan as well as online. At Mercy University we strive to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. Our Mission: Mercy University is committed to providing motivated students the opportunity to transform their lives through higher education by offering liberal arts and professional programs in personalized and high-quality learning environments, thus preparing students to embark on rewarding careers, to continue learning throughout their lives and to act ethically and responsibly in a changing world. Benefits Eligible: Mercy University strives to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. EEO Statement Mercy University is an equal opportunity employer. Mercy University actively engages in recruiting a diverse workforce and student body that includes members of historically underrepresented groups and strives to build and sustain a welcoming and supportive campus community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, pregnancy, height, weight, genetic information, disability, or protected veteran status. As part of this commitment, Mercy University will ensure that persons with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations for the hiring process. If reasonable 