    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/associate-director-university-advisement-a00207-dobbs-ferry-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director, University Advisement- A00207",
      "description": "Associate Director, University Advisement- A00207 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Associate Director, University Advisement- A00207 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Associate Director, University Advisement- A00207 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Faculty Full-time Staff Full-time $68,000-$70,000 annually Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Associate Director of University Advisement is responsible for being highly accessible, integrating services and programs in academic advising, student intervention and support, professional integrations for student development, academic integrations for student development, and social integration for student development. The Associate Director supervises a team of staff that will also provide these services in a detailed and tailored approach, positing mentorship as a key relationship dynamic and providing an intentional standard of care. These services and programs will support student success, self-efficacy, and a transformational college experience, maximizing the student-centered approach and deepening connection to the Mercy University community through all years of enrollment matriculation. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Support students in their transition to the University and integrate new students into the academic, social, and professional aspects of the University, resulting in improved retention and graduation outcomes. Provide academic advisement of students, specifically through the progression of the initial deposit and registration upon acceptance to major/degree selection as it pertains to academic and professional pursuits. Provide cohort intervention programs and lead student achievement planning for probation statuses, dismissals, and other potential departures from the University. Intervene with holistic advice on matters regarding college student readiness, which includes but is not limited to financial literacy, academic readiness, and preparatory characteristics, to identify solutions for student success. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and administrators to coordinate academic advising services across various disciplines and departments. Assist in the development and execution of advising-related initiatives, including orientation programs, academic workshops, and advising campaigns. Lead and manage professional development initiatives, ensuring team members have access to relevant training opportunities to enhance skills, foster growth, and improve overall performance. Support students' career exploration resources and advisement, resulting in a timely career track relative/paralleled to academic pursuits. Provide student engagement programs and services, resulting in a quality experience for Mercy students. Work specifically with the assigned student caseload portfolio. Assist in evaluating strategies and programs and implement changes as necessary. Hire, train, and manage staff performance. Provide opportunities for engagement through clubs and activities. Any other related duties as assigned Required Skills & Experience: Minimum 5 years of approximately related experience required. Experience in student services and advisement will be given preference. Minimum 2 years’ supervisory experience is required. Education Requirements: Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. Apply Now First Name (required) 6f4b6544 Last Name (required) d92545d7 Email (required) 7c2e81bd Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 3fab4352 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Admissions & Recruitment Admissions & Recruitment Locations Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States First Na