    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/executive-director-data-analytics-a00745-tarrytown-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Data Analytics- A00745",
      "description": "Executive Director, Data Analytics- A00745 - Tarrytown, New York, United States Executive Director, Data Analytics- A00745 - Tarrytown, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Executive Director, Data Analytics- A00745 Tarrytown, New York, United States Staff Full-time $110,000 - $122,000 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: Mercy University seeks a creative data analytics leader for an exciting role leading the University's efforts to sustain and grow a culture of data use to support decision making that leads to increased rates of student success. The role requires equal parts - technical expertise using data analytics, business intelligence, statistical modeling, and data mining, - communication skills to transform data into actionable information, generating useful insights in partnership with colleagues across the institution, - and leadership to identify and scope analytics projects and support junior analysts. The selected candidate will be tenacious about finding answers to questions - and coming up with the right questions - that will help to achieve better outcomes and will share Mercy's commitment to transformative experiences for the students and communities we serve. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Every effort has been made to identify the essential functions of this position. It in no way states or implies that the responsibilities listed are the only duties required to perform in this position. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position responsibilities if the work is similar, related, or is an essential function of the position. Data Analytics & Institutional Planning Conduct research studies in areas related to the University’s strategic objectives and student learning outcomes, and in support of the University’s planning initiatives. Deliver in-depth analytics and reporting to support decision-making by and among VPs, deans, directors and other stakeholders. Analyze, distribute and present information for use in planning, decision-making, internal and external reporting and policy formulation at the University. Use longitudinal data from external and internal sources to develop analytics for initiatives and program evaluations. Manage data analysts and reporting staff to ensure timely reporting and delivery of ad-hoc data requests. Build a culture of data-supported decision-making across the University, enabling others to develop basic data proficiency to conduct independent studies and ensure accuracy. With the AVP AI, Data, and Institutional Strategy (Chief Data and Analytics Officer), identify tools, technologies, and services to further enhance the analytics capabilities of the University (and its individual offices and divisions) and drive the integration of these tools/systems. Oversee design, implementation and analysis of internal surveys. Develop advanced analytical and business intelligence capabilities to support the University’s expanding need for data-driven, strategic and operational decision-making. Develop data dashboards and visualizations in partnership with departments and programs. Maintain fluency with trends in higher education to keep the University current with evolving national practices. Data Governance & Data Integrity Develop enterprise-wide, integrated data governance program designed to optimize the University’s use of data and information assets. Collaborate with Information Technology team to implement security measures to ensure user access is appropriate. Collaborate with stakeholders in the development of a standardized approach for reporting University metrics. Ensure that process is documented. Ensure data integrity across applicable platforms and take efforts to correct erroneous data. Develop and improve existing processes and make suggestions to streamline through the automation and documentation of tasks. Maintain fluency with trends in higher education regarding collection, analysis, and reporting practices to keep the University current with evolving national practices. General Management With the Director of Institutional Reporting & Compliance, provide strategic direction and oversight for the Office of Institutional Research. Develop and advance a strong partnership network among deans, directors and other stakeholders, as well as the assessment offices. Desired Characteristics: Disciplined, structured and data-driven approach to decision-making and problem solving with a sharp focus on metrics, outcomes and results Action-oriented, collaborative, adaptable and innovative approach to work Demonstrated understanding of data architecture, data management and the development of data governance Ability to synthesize and communicate complex concepts to a broad spectrum of stakeholders Demonstrated ability to lead and cultivate a proactive, inclusive, results-oriented work environment High level of integrity, accountability and superior judgement Core Qualifications: Minimum of 5-years' experience of progressively responsible experience in data analytics or business intelligence, data analysis, program evaluation, institutional research, or related research practices, with preference for a candidate with higher education experience. At least 1-2 years in a leadership role in data or analytics. Proficiency with research design, statistical procedures and analysis. Ability to conduct quantitative and qualitative research, including design, data collection, analysis and reporting. Proficiency with data visualization software like Tableau. Power BI, etc. Experience working with large databases, including extracting, evaluating and manipulating data for reporting and analytical purposes using query tools and/or programming language (e.g., SQL). Use of higher education dataset and tools such as IPEDS and the National Student Clearinghouse. Experience with leading an enterprise data transformation project and/or with data culture transformation. Education Required: Bachelor's degree in Business Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Engineering, Management, or related field. Master's preferred. Apply Now First Name (required) a26a3cfc Last Name (required) 051bfc50 Email (required) 5b905d5c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 0d2767b6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Locations Tarrytown, New York, United States Tarrytown, New York, United States First Name (required) 72c8a2ba Last Name (required) 5abc5ce7 Email (required) 022b4a66 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner (NP) with academic leadership experience who can simultaneously steward program quality, contribute to the development of new programs, cultivate meaningful clinical and academic partnerships, and contribute to the School’s strategic direction. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00559) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This p