    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/student-worker-school-of-education-ce0064-dobbs-ferry-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Student Worker, School of Education- CE0064",
      "description": "Student Worker, School of Education- CE0064 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Student Worker, School of Education- CE0064 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Student Worker, School of Education- CE0064 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Student worker $17.00/hour Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary The School of Education at Mercy University is seeking a reliable, organized, and detail-oriented student worker to provide administrative and office support to the Associate Deans at the Dobbs Ferry campus. The student worker will assist with office operations and provide general administrative support to help ensure the School of Education’s academic activities run smoothly. This position provides professional experience in an academic administrative environment while developing skills in communication, organization, customer service, and office management. Essential Responsibilities The Student Worker may assist with the following duties: Provide general administrative and clerical support to the Associate Deans. Organize, file, scan, and maintain documents and office records. Assist with preparing materials, correspondence, forms, reports, and presentations. Respond to routine inquiries from students, faculty, staff, and visitors and direct questions to the appropriate office or staff member. Assist with scheduling meetings, preparing meeting materials, and maintaining calendars as directed. Support School of Education events, meetings, orientations, and other activities. Assist with data entry and updating spreadsheets, databases, and departmental records. Help maintain an organized and welcoming office environment. Sort and distribute mail and other materials as needed. Assist with special projects and other administrative tasks assigned by the Associate Deans. Ability to work at the Dobbs Ferry campus. The specific work schedule will be arranged based on the student worker's class schedule and the needs of the School of Education. Qualifications Current Mercy University student in good academic standing. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Professional and courteous communication skills. Ability to work independently and follow directions. Attention to detail and accuracy. Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace, including email, Word/Docs, and Excel/Sheets. Ability to maintain confidentiality when handling student, faculty, or administrative information. Previous office, customer service, or administrative experience is helpful but not required. Skills and Competencies The successful candidate will demonstrate: Reliability and punctuality Professionalism Attention to detail Organization and follow-through Effective written and verbal communication Ability to prioritize multiple tasks Willingness to learn and take initiative Ability to work respectfully with students, faculty, staff, and visitors Apply Now First Name (required) 3b2f1167 Last Name (required) cb817c10 Email (required) 7d120abb Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert c1a9b216 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Education School of Education Locations Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 8f2cd989 Last Name (required) 48b7e907 Email (required) b74b863d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursin