    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-student-financial-services-a00217-manhattan-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Financial Services- A00217",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Student Financial Services- A00217 - Manhattan, New York, United States Assistant Director of Student Financial Services- A00217 - Manhattan, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Assistant Director of Student Financial Services- A00217 Manhattan, New York, United States Staff Full-time $55,000–$57,500 annually Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: Under the direction of the Senior Assistant Director of Student Financial Services, the Assistant Director of Student Financial Services will assist in the management of the daily operations of the Student Financial Services Offices to support the Campus Operations ensuring the professional, efficient and compliant processing of student records. The Assistant Director of Student Financial Services will assist in the management of the supervision of registration processes, resulting billing processes, and counseling of students and families. The Assistant Director of Student Financial Services will also serve as a primary supervisor of the Student Financial Services Counselors, ensuring student centered service in meeting the needs of traditional, non-traditional, adult and minority student populations. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Assist in the management of the daily workflow of the Student Financial Services staff; assist in the coordination of projects and assignments from the Systems Management Operations staff, the Business Operations staff, and the Student Financial Services staff, in an organized and consistent manner as outlined by the Vice President and the Executive Director. Assist in the management of all advising related activities; process & analyze on a term by term basis degree audit for respective cohort. Review and communicate with student on term by term basis requirements leading towards degree, developing successful education plan for respective students. Counsel students and families, detailing the Student Financial Services processes, including but not limited to student admissions eligibility, student aid eligibility, SAP requirements, enrollment requirements, packaging policies, registration & subsequent billing processes, and R2T4 calculations, etc. Demonstrate knowledge of financial aid regulations, along with registration, enrollment, disbursement and refund (financial aid related) regulations. Must keep abreast of ever changing federal, state, and institutional regulations and policies; ensure institutional policies and procedures are updated on a regular and consistent basis; ensure supporting staff are trained as regulations are updated. Complete Department of Education Verification processes for those selected. Very those with conflicting data. Make appropriate ‘professional judgments’ for those with special circumstances utilizing knowledge of detailed financial aid regulations and related experience. Manage registration, loan certification, and related outreach and processing efforts of subordinate Student Financial Services staff members. Assist in the management of the review and development processes of newly developing and existing degree audits, ensuring accurate advising and degree planning processes for students. Process daily payment and related receipts; including, not exclusively, book store voucher processes; collect resulting registration payments; issue appropriate receipts; post appropriate payments; issue applicable receipts; reconcile daily receipts; process refund requests and account corrections; sell parking permits; accept payments for special services. In coordination with the Senior Assistant Director of Student Financial Services, provide supervisory management of Student Financial Services Counseling Staff members at the campus locations; disseminate weekly, outreach and processing assignments; coordinate feedback of said assignments with the Offices of Systems Management Operations, Business Operations and the Vice President. Process daily, term based, and annual registration related items, including but not limited to Census processes, NOA review processes, Grading Closeout processes, transfer credit processes, degree audit processes. Additionally, ensure aid eligibility and payment compliance is adhered as related to registration compliance, including but not limited to R2T4 calculations, return of funds, disbursement eligibility, etc. Work with Program chairpersons and faculty to address individual student academic concerns; encourage students to connect with faculty within program, exploring opportunities (internships, research projects, graduate school, etc). Refer students to College and community support services as needed. Assist with comprehensive registration and graduation related processes, ensuring timeliness and accurate processing as related to scheduling, transcript request generation, transfer credit processes, grading follow up processes, graduation follow up processes, bulletin development, etc. Hire, train, supervise and manage the performance of staff to meet departmental and division objectives. Assure adequate staffing of department. Manage all vacation, sick and personal time of the Student Financial Services staff in the absence of the Director of Student Financial Services. Ensure performance appraisals are appropriately completed and submitted in a timely fashion to the Vice President and Human Resources. Participate in the design, implementation, and coordination of various resource management projects. Perform various tasks as assigned for Enrollment Management activities, such as: Open House, Accepted Students Days, Scholarship Events, etc. Attend all departmental staff meetings and training sessions. Perform other duties and projects as assigned. Required Skills & Experience: Minimum of two to three years experience with financial aid/bursar (registrar a plus) with at least one year in a managerial capacity Must be proficient in Banner, the internet, Microsoft Office Suite, and multiple Department of Education software products. Broad knowledge of financial aid specific and related regulations (federal and state) required. Demonstrated leadership, interpersonal, written and oral communication, problem-solving, organizational, and presentation skills. Demonstrated evidence of detail-orientation, customer service orientation, ability to work independently, ability to manage great levels of responsibility required. Bi-lingual (Spanish) a plus. Ability to work long hours, including weekends and evenings as required. Prior experience with publications and data research desirable. Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Candidates for hire will be required to sign a waiver authorizing the background check. Ability to Travel Education Requirements: Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. Apply Now First Name (required) dd1e33ea Last Name (required) 0c94bac7 Email (required) e9a3b739 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 99aa7f40 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Office of Student Financial Service Office of Student Financial Service Locations Manhattan, New York, United States Manhattan, New York, United States First Name (required) 19a9455d Last Name (required) cabb6c2e Email (required) 394dd927 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner (NP) with academic leadership experience who can simultaneou