    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/men-s-lacrosse-coaches-ml3727-dobbs-ferry-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Men's Lacrosse Coaches- ML3727",
      "description": "Men's Lacrosse Coaches- ML3727 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Men's Lacrosse Coaches- ML3727 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Men's Lacrosse Coaches- ML3727 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Part-Time $5000-$8000 Add to favorites View favorites Join Our Team: Staff Part-Time Men's Lacrosse Coach Mercy University seeks a passionate and experienced Staff Part-Time Men's Lacrosse Coach to join our Admissions & Recruitment team. This unique position combines coaching excellence with student recruitment, offering an opportunity to shape both athletic and academic success for prospective student-athletes. About the Opportunity As a Staff Part-Time Men's Lacrosse Coach, you'll work directly with our admissions team to identify, recruit, and develop talented student-athletes who align with Mercy University's values and academic standards. You'll play an essential role in building our men's lacrosse program while supporting our commitment to student success both on and off the field. Key Responsibilities Recruit qualified student-athletes through high school visits, tournaments, and showcases Collaborate with admissions counselors to evaluate prospective students Conduct coaching sessions and skill development programs Build relationships with high school coaches and lacrosse organizations Support current team members with academic and athletic guidance Represent Mercy University at recruitment events and community functions What We're Looking For Bachelor's degree required Previous lacrosse coaching or playing experience at competitive levels Strong communication and interpersonal skills Experience in student recruitment or admissions preferred Understanding of NCAA regulations and compliance standards Ability to work flexible hours including evenings and weekends Commitment to supporting student-athlete academic achievement Why Mercy University Join a supportive community that values diversity, inclusion, and personal growth. Our collaborative environment encourages innovation in both athletics and academics. You'll work alongside dedicated professionals who share your passion for student development and competitive excellence. We offer competitive compensation, professional development opportunities, and the chance to make a meaningful impact on young athletes' lives and futures. Ready to help build something special? We encourage applications from candidates of all backgrounds who share our commitment to student success and inclusive excellence. Apply Now First Name (required) 4de4f97c Last Name (required) 71725c15 Email (required) 7da1a0e8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 4c4c1fd4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Athletics Athletics Locations Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 8322e4cc Last Name (required) 8f41ccdf Email (required) 43d0771e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner (NP) with academic leadership experience who can simultaneously steward program quality, contribute to the development of new programs, cultivate meaningful clinical and academic partnerships, and contribute to the School’s strategic direction. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00559) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positi