    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/simulation-lab-assistant-bronx-lb4120-bronx-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Simulation Lab Assistant - Bronx- LB4120",
      "description": "Simulation Lab Assistant - Bronx- LB4120 - Bronx, New York, United States Simulation Lab Assistant - Bronx- LB4120 - Bronx, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Simulation Lab Assistant - Bronx- LB4120 Bronx, New York, United States Staff Part-Time $20.00 - $25.00 per hour Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Simulation Lab Assistant provides crucial operational, technical, and administrative support to the Simulation Center and the Director of Simulation. This role ensures the smooth daily operation of the nursing simulation labs, prepares high-fidelity and low-fidelity environments for student experiences, manages specialized inventory, and assists faculty and students during active simulation scenarios, skill labs, and objective structured clinical examinations (OSCEs). Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Every effort has been made to identify the essential functions of this position. It in no way states or implies that the responsibilities listed are the only duties required to perform in this position. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position responsibilities if the work is similar, related, or is an essential function of the position. Operations & Lab Preparation Scenario Setup & Teardown: Physically prepare simulation rooms, task trainers, and high-fidelity mannequins according to specific course objectives and faculty blueprints (e.g., setting up moulage, IV lines, medications, and clinical props). Clean and reset the rooms efficiently between sessions Technology Readiness: Power up, test, and troubleshoot simulators, audio-visual recording systems (such as Zoom Education, CAE, or Laerdal systems), and electronic health record (EHR) software prior to student arrival Environment Realism: Maintain an authentic clinical environment, ensuring that patient care bays look identical to a live hospital or outpatient setting Inventory, Procurement, & Maintenance Stock Management: Track consumable clinical supplies (such as syringes, PPE, gauze, and IV tubing), noting when items run low and preparing orders for approval Vendor Coordination: Assist in organizing quotes and documentation for medical equipment and simulator maintenance contracts (working with vendors such as McKesson, Medline, or MedShipment) Equipment Care: Perform routine preventative maintenance, cleaning, and proper storage of high-fidelity mannequins and delicate task trainers to maximize their lifespan Instructional & Faculty Support In-Sim Assistance: Serve as a standardized patient, embedded participant (voice of the patient), or operate the simulator control software during active mock codes or clinical scenarios Student Safety & Guidance: Monitor students for safe equipment usage in the lab during open lab hours or independent practice sessions Required Skills & Experience: Previous experience specifically within a healthcare simulation lab Familiarity with healthcare terminology, basic medical supplies, and standard patient safety protocols Education Requirements: Bachelors degree or in a healthcare, technology, or administrative field (or equivalent combination of education and clinical environment experience) Apply Now First Name (required) f34959ba Last Name (required) a844c60e Email (required) 9581a356 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert e07ec680 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Nursing School of Nursing Locations Bronx, New York, United States Bronx, New York, United States First Name (required) 9dc41ea8 Last Name (required) d9588074 Email (required) 8296b541 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Assoc