      "title": "Assistant Volleyball Coach- VB3735",
      "description": "Assistant Volleyball Coach- VB3735 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Assistant Volleyball Coach- VB3735 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Assistant Volleyball Coach- VB3735 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Part-Time $6,000-$12,000 annually Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: Mercy University's Athletics program is looking for a dedicated Assistant Volleyball Coach to join its competitive NCAA Division II program at the Dobbs Ferry campus. If you bring hands-on coaching experience and a genuine commitment to student-athlete development, this is a meaningful opportunity to contribute to a program that takes both athletic performance and academic success seriously. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Assist in providing leadership in all aspects of assigned program Committed to compliance with the NCAA, East Coast Conference, and Mercy College regulations. Successful completion of the NCAA certification exam Assist in identifying, evaluating and recruiting academically prepared students in accordance with College policy and NCAA regulations Assist in providing academic oversight of student athletes to ensure retention and graduation Assist in arranging all aspects of scheduling, team travel, team operations etc. Maintain open and harmonious communication with facets of campus community Maintain fiscal responsibility and integrity. Maintain moral and ethical integrity Participate in community, campus, and departmental initiatives when appropriate Submission of all required requests / paperwork. In addition, commitment in following the letter and spirit of NCAA, Conference, and College rules and regulations Ability to effectively work with a diverse population of student athletes and coaches in a cultural climate that celebrates diversity Perform other duties and projects as assigned Required Skills & Experience: Knowledge of the rules of Volleyball Ability to communi