    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/asst-women-s-basketball-coach-dobbs-ferry-ny-new-york-united-states-652af42e-6695-423f-86ee-243c3c7fb02a": {
      "title": "Asst. Women's Basketball Coach",
      "description": "Asst. Women's Basketball Coach - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Asst. Women's Basketball Coach - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Asst. Women's Basketball Coach Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Part-Time $3000-$5000 Add to favorites View favorites Mercy University is looking for a knowledgeable and committed Assistant Women's Basketball Coach to join our athletics program on a part-time basis. This is a genuine opportunity to shape the development of student-athletes while contributing to a university that places people at the center of everything it does. What You'll Be Doing Support the Head Coach in planning and delivering practices, game-day preparation, and in-season player development Assist with the recruitment of prospective student-athletes, working closely with the Admissions and Recruitment team to identify and engage candidates who align with Mercy's academic and athletic standards Monitor student-athlete academic progress and provide mentorship that supports success both on and off the court Ensure all activities comply with NCAA and Northeast-10 Conference regulations What You Bring Collegiate playing or coaching experience in women's basketball Working knowledge of NCAA recruiting rules and eligibility requirements Demonstrated ability to build trust with student-athletes from diverse backgrounds Strong communication skills across in-person, digital, and recruitment settings Experience supporting academic accountability for student-athletes, consistent with Mercy University's commitment to graduating well-rounded individuals A current, valid driver's license and ability to travel for recruiting and competition Why Mercy Mercy University's mission is to provide access to higher education for students who might not otherwise have the opportunity — and that same spirit of inclusion runs through its athletics program. As part of the Mavericks community, you'll work within a program that values academic achievement as highly as athletic performance. Mercy offers staff access to professional development resources, tuition benefits, and a campus culture built on mentorship and belonging. This role offers real influence over the direction of a growing program, with direct collaboration between athletics and admissions that few institutions offer at this level. Ready to Join the Mavericks? Submit your resume and a brief cover letter outlining your coaching philosophy and recruiting experience through Mercy University's careers portal. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis, so we encourage you to apply early. Apply Now First Name (required) 55b8e345 Last Name (required) f514011d Email (required) 0d3f9bae Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 53730d3c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Admissions & Recruitment Admissions & Recruitment Locations Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) c42dd145 Last Name (required) a884a40c Email (required) 0dcc02be Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner (NP) with academic leadership experience who can simultaneously steward program quality, contribute to the development of new programs, cultivate meaningful clinical and academic partnerships, and contribute to the School’s strategic direction. Instructor/Assistant Professor, Sch