    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/assistant-women-s-soccer-coach-dobbs-ferry-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Women's Soccer Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Women's Soccer Coach - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Assistant Women's Soccer Coach - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Assistant Women's Soccer Coach Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Part-Time $3000-$5000 Add to favorites View favorites Mercy University: Unleashing Your Coaching Potential Calling all passionate soccer enthusiasts! Mercy University, located in the vibrant town of Dobbs Ferry, is seeking a dynamic and driven individual to join our Athletics team as an Assistant Women's Soccer Coach on a part-time basis. As a member of our esteemed coaching staff, you will have the opportunity to shape the minds and skills of our talented student-athletes, instilling in them the values of teamwork, discipline, and an unwavering commitment to excellence. Working alongside our experienced Head Coach, you will play a crucial role in developing game strategies, conducting engaging training sessions, and nurturing the growth of our players both on and off the field. Responsibilities: - Assist in the planning and execution of comprehensive training programs tailored to enhance players' technical, tactical, and physical abilities. - Contribute to the development of game-day strategies and in-game coaching decisions. - Foster a positive and inclusive team culture that emphasizes sportsmanship, resilience, and a commitment to academic excellence. - Provide mentorship and guidance to student-athletes, supporting their personal and professional growth. - Collaborate with the coaching staff, athletic trainers, and academic advisors to ensure a holistic approach to student-athlete development. Qualifications: - A bachelor's degree in a relevant field, with a strong background in soccer coaching and player development. - Proven experience in coaching and mentoring female athletes at the collegiate or high-level competitive youth level. - Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to motivate and inspire student-athletes. - A deep understanding of the game's tactics, strategies, and current trends. - Strong organizational and time management abilities. - A commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive environment for all student-athletes. Join our passionate team at Mercy University and be part of a thriving athletic program dedicated to nurturing the potential of our student-athletes. Apply today and embark on an exciting journey where you can shape the future of our women's soccer program and contribute to the overall success of our institution. To apply, please submit your resume, cover letter, and relevant coaching credentials to [email protected] by [deadline date]. Mercy University is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community. Apply Now First Name (required) 077b6bec Last Name (required) bab79c74 Email (required) 56623390 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert b7416864 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Athletics Athletics Locations Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) a9e23fc0 Last Name (required) 91a3d18d Email (required) 731e3edc Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner (NP) with academic leadership experience who can simultaneously steward program quality, contribute to the development of new programs, cultivate meaningful clinical and academic partnerships, and contribute to the School’s strategic direction. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00559) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This position is for the undergraduate programs that run on weekdays and weekends on the Dobbs Ferry (Westchester) and Bronx campuses. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00597) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This position is for the undergraduate programs that run on weekdays and weekends on the Dobbs Ferry (Westchester) and Bronx campuses. About Mercy Mercy University is a dynamic, independent, coeducational New York City area university that offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate degree and certificate programs in six schools: Business, Education, Health and Natural Sciences, Liberal Arts, Nursing, and Social and Behavioral Sciences. Mercy is the region's largest private, nonprofit, Minority-Serving Institution, proud to serve a student body that is highly diverse. As a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI), Mercy University, has been ranked nationally among top colleges in the country for Hispanics by the Hispanic Association of Colleges and Universities (HACU) and by Excelencia in Education, earning their prestigious Seal of Excelencia for intentionally serving Latino students. Mercy University was further recognized by HACU as a national leader in awarding bachelor's degrees to Hispanics in several disciplines, including Psychology, Sociology, and Business. Westchester Magazine has also named Mercy the Best College in Westchester County in 2019, 2020, and 2022. Mercy is committed to offering an inclusive learning environment to help a diverse student body set a course for their future. To support its student body, Mercy has been awarded a number of federal grants which enable us to better develop and deliver education to our students. Mercy’s student body reflects the rich diversity of the New York metropolitan area. Enrollment, including full-time and part-time undergraduates and graduates, is approximately 8,800. Mercy students learn on campuses in Dobbs Ferry, the Bronx, and Manhattan as well as online. At Mercy University we strive to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. Our Mission: Mercy University is committed to providing motivated students the opportunity to transform their lives through higher education by offering liberal arts and professional programs in personalized and high-quality learning environments, thus preparing students to embark on rewarding careers, to continue learning throughout their lives and to act ethically and responsibly in a changing world. Benefits Eligible: Mercy University strives to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. EEO Statement Mercy University is an equal opportunity employer. Mercy University actively engages in recruiting a diverse workforce and student body that includes members of historically underrepresented groups and strives to build and sustain a welcoming and supportive campus community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, pregnancy, height, weight, genetic information, disability, or protected veteran status. As part of this commitment, Mercy University will ensure that persons with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations for the hiring process. If reasonable accommodation is needed, please contact The Office of Human Resources at (914) 674-7839, Option 6 or via email at HR@mercy.edu. The posted salary range for this position is based on several legitimate, non-discriminatory factors set by the organization. Mercy is committed to ensuring equal pay opportunities for equal work regardless of gender, race, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local pay equity laws. Campus Safety Mercy University is committed to providing a safe and welcoming environment for all. Information regarding campus safety can be found here . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
