    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/associate-athletic-trainer-dobbs-ferry-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Associate Athletic Trainer - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Associate Athletic Trainer - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Associate Athletic Trainer Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Full-time $58,000.00 - $65,000.00 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Associate Athletic Trainer is responsible for assisting the Head Athletic Trainer in the education, prevention, evaluation, treatment, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries incurred by Mercy University intercollegiate athletes. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Every effort has been made to identify the essential functions of this position. It in no way states or implies that the responsibilities listed are the only duties required to perform in this position. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position responsibilities if the work is similar, related, or is an essential function of the position. Supervise/Provide coverage and care of teams for practices and games (will involve some travel and work on weekends) Work with the Team Physician for the Health Care of the Student Athletes Create and maintain accurate records of athletic injuries and rehabilitation Assist with administrative tasks required for athletic injury insurance claims Assist in maintaining a safe and clean Athletic Training Room Mentor interns from Mercy University’s Exercise Science Program Perform other duties as assigned Required Skills & Experience: Minimum of one (1) year experience as a practicing National Athletic Trainers Association (NATA) Board of Certification (BOC) certified Athletic Trainer is preferred Strong oral and written communication skills, as well as excellent interpersonal skills are required Education Requirements: Maintain NATA BOC certification Maintain Athletic Trainer license in the state of New York Bachelor's degree required Physical/Other Requirements: Flexibility to w