    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-communication-arts-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty- Communication Arts",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty- Communication Arts - New York, United States Adjunct Faculty- Communication Arts - New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Adjunct Faculty- Communication Arts New York, United States Faculty Part Time $3,850-$3,950 Add to favorites View favorites The Communication Arts program at Mercy University seeks part-time, adjunct instructors to teach a variety of courses to undergraduate students. Adjunct positions are filled as needed through ongoing recruitment. Applicants are contacted and hired year-round based on program needs. The Communication Arts program consists of four different areas: Communication and Culture, Strategic Communication and Writing, Content Creation and Production, and Voice and Performance. Successful candidates may be offered the opportunity to teach up to three sections of any given course. Please attach your current CV and brief cover letter outlining your experience teaching college-level courses or desire to do so. Please do not include any other documentation. Schedule & Location: Day and evening teaching opportunities. Courses may be offered at our campuses at Dobbs Ferry, Manhattan, The Bronx, or online Qualifications: Though teaching experience is preferred, expertise, professionalism, and a genuine desire to help students is far more important Education Requirements: Masters or Doctorate from an accredited institution in an appropriate academic discipline More information about the Communication Arts program and curriculum can be found on our catalog page: Mercy University Catalog Apply Now First Name (required) 109e1ef4 Last Name (required) 451ad4c1 Email (required) a83e14fd Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 423e9adc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your jo