    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-risk-management-insurance-af1122-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Risk Management & Insurance (AF1122)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty – Risk Management & Insurance (AF1122) - New York, United States Adjunct Faculty – Risk Management & Insurance (AF1122) - New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Adjunct Faculty – Risk Management & Insurance (AF1122) New York, United States Faculty Part Time $3,000.00 - $3,750.00 Add to favorites View favorites The School of Business at Mercy University invites applications for part-time adjunct faculty to teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses within the Risk Management & Insurance program. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in areas such as: Risk Management Commercial Insurance Enterprise Risk Management Claims & Loss Control Compliance & Regulatory Risk Cyber Risk Financial Risk Healthcare Risk Management Insurance Analytics Related business and insurance disciplines Adjunct faculty may be responsible for course development (where applicable) and subsequent instruction. Courses may be delivered in multiple modalities, including in-person at the Dobbs Ferry, Bronx, and Manhattan campuses, as well as online (synchronous and/or asynchronous). Successful candidates may be assigned up to three course assignments per term, based on program needs and enrollment. We seek instructors who demonstrate a strong commitment to inclusive excellence, student engagement, and applied, practice-oriented learning. Location Dobbs Ferry Campus Bronx Campus Manhattan Campus Online (synchronous and/or asynchronous) Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s and Master’s degree in risk management, Insurance, FRM Certificate, Finance, Business Administration, or a closely related field Minimum of five (5) years of professional experience in risk management, insurance, compliance, financial services, or a related field Strong communication and organizational skills Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience at the college level Industry certifications such as CPCU, ARM, CRM, CIC, or related credentials Experience with analytics, AI applications, or emerging technologies in insurance and risk management Demonstrated expertise in applied business or insurance-related practice About Mercy University Mercy University is a dynamic, independent, coeducational New York metropolitan area university serving approximately 8,800 students across campuses in Dobbs Ferry, Bronx, and Manhattan, as well as online. Mercy University is committed to providing motivated students the opportunity to transform their lives through higher education in personalized and high-quality learning environments while preparing students for rewarding careers and lifelong learning. EEO Statement Mercy University is an equal opportunity employer. Mercy University actively engages in recruiting a diverse workforce and student body and strives to build and sustain a welcoming and supportive campus community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, protected veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Apply Now First Name (required) 3d0d2ac5 Last Name (required) b39016df Email (required) 91a8670a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 8967687e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Business School of Business Locations New York, United States New York, United States First Name (required) 959a6cbd Last Name (required) 4db6575d Email (required) e6e4afcc Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner (NP) with academic leadership experience who can simultaneously steward program quality, contribute to the development of new programs, cultivate meaningful clinical and academic partnerships, and contribute to the School’s strategic direction. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00559) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This position is for the undergraduate programs that run on weekdays and weekends on the Dobbs Ferry (Westchester) and Bronx campuses. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00597) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This position is for the undergraduate programs that run on weekdays and weekends on the Dobbs Ferry (Westchester) and Bronx campuses. About Mercy Mercy University is a dynamic, independent, coeducational New York City area university that offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate degree and certificate programs in six schools: Business, Education, Health and Natural Sciences, Liberal Arts, Nursing, and Social and Behavioral Sciences. Mercy is the region's largest private, nonprofit, Minority-Serving Institution, proud to serve a student body that is highly diverse. As a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI), Mercy University, has been ranked nationally among top colleges in the country for Hispanics by the Hispanic Association of Colleges and Universities (HACU) and by Excelencia in Education, earning their prestigious Seal of Excelencia for intentionally serving Latino students. Mercy University was further recognized by HACU as a national leader in awarding bachelor's degrees to Hispanics in several disciplines, including Psychology, Sociology, and Business. Westchester Magazine has also named Mercy the Best College in Westchester County in 2019, 2020, and 2022. Mercy is committed to offering an inclusive learning environment to help a diverse student body set a course for their future. To support its student body, Mercy has been awarded a number of federal grants which enable us to better develop and deliver education to our students. Mercy’s student body reflects the rich diversity of the New York metropolitan area. Enrollment, including full-time and part-time undergraduates and graduates, is approximately 8,800. Mercy students learn on campuses in Dobbs Ferry, the Bronx, and Manhattan as well as online. At Mercy University we strive to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. Our Mission: Mercy University is committed to providing motivated students the opportunity to transform their lives through higher education by offering liberal arts and professional programs in personalized and high-quality learning environments, thus preparing students to embark on rewarding careers, to continue learning throughout their lives and to act ethically and responsibly in a changing world. Benefits Eligible: Mercy University strives to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. EEO Statement Mercy University is an equal opportunity employer. Mercy University actively engages in recruiting a diverse workforce and student body that includes members of historically underrepresented groups and strives to build and sustain a welcoming and supportive campus community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, pregnancy, height, weight, genetic information, disability, or protected veteran status. As part of this commitment, Mercy University will ensure that persons with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations for the hiring process. If reasonable accommodation is needed, please contact The Office of Human Resources at (914) 674-7839, Option 6 or via email at HR@mercy.edu. The posted salary range for this position is based on several legitimate, non-discriminatory factors set by the organization. Mercy is committed to ensuring equal pay opportunities for equal work regardless of gender, race, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local pay equity laws. Campus Safety Mercy University is committed to providing a safe and welcoming environment for all. Information regarding campus safety can be found here . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
