    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/associate-director-clinical-simulation-lab-a00531-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Clinical Simulation Lab (A00531)",
      "description": "Associate Director, Clinical Simulation Lab (A00531) - New York, United States Associate Director, Clinical Simulation Lab (A00531) - New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Associate Director, Clinical Simulation Lab (A00531) New York, United States Staff Full-time $75,000 to $85,000 annually Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Associate Director of the Clinical Simulation Laboratory provides support for all simulation and clinical learning laboratory experiences in collaboration with faculty and staff to manage and supervise the clinical operations in the School of Nursing Department’s Clinical Simulation Center. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Every effort has been made to identify the essential functions of this position. It in no way states or implies that the responsibilities listed are the only duties required to perform in this position. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position responsibilities if the work is similar, related, or is an essential function of the position. Manages daily activities and services of the Bronx Clinical Simulation Lab, including: scheduling and conducting clinical simulations, lab set up, lab breakdown, and management of lab equipment and supplies. Supports the planning and utilization of skills & simulation in the Nursing program. Assists instructors and/or students in a clinical lab setting. Ensures that the lab/classroom is clean, safe, and organized; promotes safe lab practices. (i.e.) washing sheets. Repairs or coordinates the repair of lab equipment as required. Collaborates with faculty to ensure the Center’s experiences meet course objectives; provide oversight during student practice and remediation on technical skills. Maintains, coordinates, and monitors open lab sessions. Operates the patient simulator during simulation sessions. Participates and assesses debriefing sessions with instructors following skill & simulation sessions to ensure best practices Researches, evaluates, and recommends new lab materials, equipment, and experiments. Implements simulation activities as required. Establishes and updates laboratory policies and procedures. Assists in preparation and maintenance of a variety of records. Assists in preparing reports as needed for nursing learning lab. Stay current with developments in the field of simulation technology and learning theories. Participates in planning, monitoring, and scheduling for students and faculty by ensuring open and structured lab utilization times are available, communicated, and appropriately resourced. Performs other duties as assigned. OR Other duties may be assigned. Required Skills & Experience: NYS Registered Nurse License Clinical Simulation Certification (CHSOS/CHSE) Work experience managing a medical skills learning lab. Recent medical surgical experience. Safety standards and practices used in lab/classroom settings. Use of Artificial Intelligence in simulation. Education Requirements: Bachelors of Science Degree from an accredited institution required. Physical/Other Requirements: Must be able to push, pull, move or lift up to 50 lbs. Must be able to meet all general health requirements for the position as per university policies Apply Now First Name (required) cf954bbe Last Name (required) 9a663eed Email (required) c0285d3d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert a2eda054 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Nursing School of Nursing Locations New York, United States New York, United States First Name (required) 1c240543 Last Name (required) cb647ef3 Email (required) f2a2c68b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner (NP) with academic leadership experience who can simultaneously steward program quality, contribute to the development of new programs, cultivate meaningful clinical and academic partnerships, and contribute to the School’s strategic direction. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00559) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This position is for the undergraduate programs that run on weekdays and weekends on the Dobbs Ferry (Westchester) and Bronx campuses. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00597) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This position is for the undergraduate programs that run on weekdays and weekends on the Dobbs Ferry (Westchester) and Bronx campuses. About Mercy Mercy University is a dynamic, independent, coeducational New York City area university that offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate degree and certificate programs in six schools: Business, Education, Health and Natural Sciences, Liberal Arts, Nursing, and Social and Behavioral Sciences. Mercy is the region's largest private, nonprofit, Minority-Serving Institution, proud to serve a student body that is highly diverse. As a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI), Mercy University, has been ranked nationally among top colleges in the country for Hispanics by the Hispanic Association of Colleges and Universities (HACU) and by Excelencia in Education, earning their prestigious Seal of Excelencia for intentionally serving Latino students. Mercy University was further recognized by HACU as a national leader in awarding bachelor's degrees to Hispanics in several disciplines, including Psychology, Sociology, and Business. Westchester Magazine has also named Mercy the Best College in Westchester County in 2019, 2020, and 2022. Mercy is committed to offering an inclusive learning environment to help a diverse student body set a course for their future. To support its student body, Mercy has been awarded a number of federal grants which enable us to better develop and deliver education to our students. Mercy’s student body reflects the rich diversity of the New York metropolitan area. Enrollment, including full-time and part-time undergraduates and graduates, is approximately 8,800. Mercy students learn on campuses in Dobbs Ferry, the Bronx, and Manhattan as well as online. At Mercy University we strive to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. Our Mission: Mercy University is committed to providing motivated students the opportunity to transform their lives through higher education by offering liberal arts and professional programs in personalized and high-quality learning environments, thus preparing students to embark on rewarding careers, to continue learning throughout their lives and to act ethically and responsibly in a changing world. Benefits Eligible: Mercy University strives to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. EEO Statement Mercy University is an equal opportunity employer. Mercy University actively engages in recruiting a diverse workforce and student body that includes members of historically underrepresented groups and strives to build and sustain a welcoming and supportive campus community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, pregnancy, height, weight, genetic information, disability, or protected veteran status. As part of this commitment, Mercy University will ensure that persons with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations for the hiring process. If reasonable accommodation is needed, please contact The Office of Human Resources at (914) 674-7839, Option 6 or via email at HR@mercy.edu. The posted salary range for this position is based on several legitimate, non-discriminatory factors set by the organization. Mercy is committed to ensuring equal pay opportunities for equal work regardless of gender, race, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local pay equity laws. Campus Safety Mercy University is committed to providing a safe and welcoming environment for all. Information regarding campus safety can be found here . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
