      "description": "Adjunct Faculty- Art and Music - New York, United States Adjunct Faculty- Art and Music - New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Adjunct Faculty- Art and Music New York, United States Faculty Part Time $3,750 Adjunct/Art and Music instructor in The Communication and the Arts department The Communication and the Arts Department at Mercy University seeks part-time, adjunct instructors to teach general education courses to undergraduate students. Successful candidates may be offered the opportunity to teach up to three sections of any given course, with an emphasis in Music and Art, with a maximum of three course assignments per semester. Commitment to teaching with inclusive excellence is required. Candidates may also be asked to provide assistance with program assessment and development and to attend select programmatic or professional development meetings. Schedule: Day and Evening teaching opportunities. Location: Courses may be offered at the Dobbs Ferry, Manhattan, or Bronx campuses, or online. Please attach a CV and a cover letter outlining your experience teaching college-level courses, and include the names, addresses, and telephone numbers of three professional references. Please upload all documents as one file. Please do not include any other documentation. Candidates should also provide a statement of scholarly interests. Qualifications • Master’s or Doctorate from an accredited institution in an appropriate academic discipline. • Demonstrated experience successfully teaching general education, Communication, Media, Music or Arts courses at the college level. Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner 