    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-and-clinical-director-counseling-f00268-dobbs-ferry-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor and Clinical Director, Counseling (F00268)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor and Clinical Director, Counseling (F00268) - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Assistant Professor and Clinical Director, Counseling (F00268) - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Assistant Professor and Clinical Director, Counseling (F00268) Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Faculty Full-time $72,000 - $77,000 Job Summary: The School of Social and Behavioral Sciences at Mercy University invites applications for a full-time, multi-year Assistant Professor/Clinical Director of Counseling position in the Department of Counseling, overseeing field experience for the School Counseling and Mental Health Counseling programs. This is an exciting opportunity to join a dedicated and engaged team as the Department of Counseling prepares CACREP accreditation to further strengthen its graduate programs and student outcomes. The Clinical Director role includes an additional stipend and a course release to support administrative and programmatic responsibilities associated with field experience coordination. This position requires regular on-campus presence. Limited flexibility for remote work may be available in alignment with departmental needs and responsibilities. We welcome dynamic educators who bring professional experience and a passion for student mentorship to make a difference in the lives of our diverse student body and the counseling profession. Mercy University is a nonsectarian, nonprofit New York metropolitan area institution offering over 90 undergraduate and graduate programs. Mercy proudly serves a diverse student population of approximately 9,000 and is a Federally designated Hispanic-Serving Institution. Faculty at Mercy are committed to providing students access to a transformative education through academic quality, innovative teaching, and robust student support. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Field Experience Coordination: Oversee practicum and internship placements for the School Counseling and Mental Health Counseling programs, including responsibility for ensuring students are appropriately placed in qualified training sites that meet program and accreditation standards. Teaching Responsibilities: The standard graduate faculty teaching load is 21 credits (7 courses) per academic year. This position includes a course release to support administrative and programmatic responsibilities related to the Clinical Director role. Teaching assignments will focus on field experience courses such as Practicum and Internship. Grant-Funded Initiatives: Provide opportunities for student engagement in grant-supported programs, including program development and student support services. Student Placement & Site Relations: Lead and manage the practicum and internship placement process, including working directly with students to secure and finalize appropriate field placements that align with program requirements. Maintain consistent communication with clinical sites and oversee the placement process from initial coordination through completion of the field experience. Partnership Development: Lead the development and maintenance of partnerships with PK–12 schools and mental health agencies to support School Counseling and Mental Health Counseling student placements. Identify, cultivate, and sustain new site relationships that align with program goals and ensure access to high-quality, supervised field experiences. Student Advising & Mentorship: Advise and mentor graduate students, fostering their academic and professional development. Program Development & Accreditation: Collaborate on program assessment, curriculum development, and efforts related to CACREP accreditation to maintain and enhance program quality. Preferred Skills: Experience teaching in online and hybrid formats. Experience working with diverse student populations. Proficiency with Learning Management Systems such as Blackboard Required Skills & Experience: A doctoral degree (Ph.D. or equivalent) in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited program. Credentialing as a certified School Counselor and/or Licensed Mental Health Counselor; credentialing in both areas is preferred. Minimum of five years of relevant field experience as a School Counselor and/or Mental Health Counselor, with experience in both settings preferred. Experience teaching graduate-level courses, particularly field experience courses such as practicum and internship in School Counseling and/or Mental Health Counseling. Demonstrated ability to coordinate, manage, and support student practicum and internship placements. Ability to build partnerships with schools, agencies, and clinical sites. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, and community partners in support of program and student success. Commitment to fostering an inclusive and multicultural learning environment. Education Requirements: PhD in Counseling from a CACREP accredited institution. Current licensure and/or certification as a School Counselor and/or LMHC in New York State or eligibility for licensure in New York State. Additional Information: This position offers a collaborative academic environment with opportunities for innovation, interdisciplinary engagement, and professional growth. As a full-time core faculty member, the selected candidate may not hold concurrent full-time employment at another institution. Application Instructions: Interested applicants should submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Teaching philosophy Evidence of teaching effectiveness (if available) Official Transcripts Names and contact information for three professional references Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Apply Now First Name (required) 9394f58f Last Name (required) 489d5085 Email (required) c9672546 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 587423c2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Social & Behavorial Sci School of Social & Behavorial Sci Locations Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 9d630b8b Last Name (required) edf167b9 Email (required) 6018b01f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Graduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing -F00630 The Graduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing reports to the Sr. Associate Dean/Chief Nursing Officer and provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in graduate nursing education. Mercy University School of Nursing seeks a nurse practitioner (NP) with academic leadership experience who can simultaneously steward program quality, contribute to the development of new programs, cultivate meaningful clinical and academic partnerships, and contribute to the School’s strategic direction. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00559) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty positions in the nursing program. This is an opportunity to join an engaged team of professional and dedicated colleagues in a CCNE-accredited program that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees. We welcome dynamic educators to our team who want to make a difference in students’ lives and in their profession. Faculty with experience teaching pathophysiology, pharmacology, or medical-surgical nursing are encouraged to apply. This position is for the undergraduate programs that run on weekdays and weekends on the Dobbs Ferry (Westchester) and Bronx campuses. Instructor/Assistant Professor, School of Nursing (F00597) Mercy University invites nominations and applications for 9-month core faculty posi