      "title": "Course Facilitators- Doctorate of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Course Facilitators- Doctorate of Physical Therapy - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Course Facilitators- Doctorate of Physical Therapy - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Course Facilitators- Doctorate of Physical Therapy Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Part-Time $50 - $65 Job Summary: Mercy University’s DPT program is looking for course facilitators to assist with specific courses. Individuals must be licensed physical therapists with or without board certified ABPTS specialization. Course facilitators will assist in the labs and practical skills competency tests as well as potentially giving some lectures or demonstrations. They may also be asked to assist outside of the classroom for review sessions or other events to improve student success. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Assist primary course faculty with instructing and supervising students in practical skills labs in the areas of musculoskeletal, neuromuscular or cardiovascular & pulmonary physical therapy. Course facilitators will observe students performing skills and provide constructive feedback. They may be asked to assist with lecture, patient simulations or to give demonstrations in front of a group of students. Every effort has been made to identify the essential functions of this position. It in no way states or implies that the responsibilities listed are the only duties required to perform in this position. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position responsibilities if the work is similar, related, or is an essential function of the position. Required Skills & Experience: Two years’ clinical experience in an outpatient, acute or subacute or inpatient hospital or other specialty setting Experience serving as a clinical instructor in the clinical setting is strongly desired Education Requirements: Graduation from a CAPTE accredited physical therapy program Ac