    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/associate-director-university-advisement-a00515-dobbs-ferry-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director, University Advisement- A00515",
      "description": "Associate Director, University Advisement- A00515 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Associate Director, University Advisement- A00515 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Associate Director, University Advisement- A00515 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Full-time $68,000-$70,000 Job Summary: The Associate Director of University Advisement is responsible for being highly accessible, integrating services and programs in academic advising, student intervention and support, professional integrations for student development, academic integrations for student development, and social integration for student development. The Associate Director supervises a team of staff that will also provide these services in a detailed and tailored approach, positing mentorship as a key relationship dynamic and providing an intentional standard of care. These services and programs will support student success, self-efficacy, and a transformational college experience, maximizing the student-centered approach and deepening connection to the Mercy University community through all years of enrollment matriculation. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Every effort has been made to identify the essential functions of this position. It does not state or imply that the responsibilities listed are the only duties required to perform in this position. The omission of specific statements of duties does not exclude them from the position responsibilities if the work is similar, related, or is an essential function of the position. • Support students in their transition to the University and integrate new students into the academic, social, and professional aspects of the University, resulting in improved retention and graduation outcomes. • Provide the academic advisement of students, specifically through the progression of the initial deposit and registration upon acceptance to major/degree selection as it pertains to academic and professional pursuits. • Provide cohort intervention programs and lead student achievement planning for probation statuses, dismissals, and other potential departures from the University. • Intervene with holistic advice on matters regarding college student readiness, which includes but is not limited to financial literacy, academic readiness, and preparatory characteristics, to identify solutions for student success. • Support students' career exploration resources and advisement, resulting in a timely career track relative/paralleled to academic pursuits. • Provide student engagement programs and services, resulting in a quality experience for Mercy students. • Work specifically with the assigned student caseload portfolio. • Assist in evaluating strategies and programs and implement changes as necessary. • Hire, train, and manage staff performance. • Provide opportunities for engagement through clubs and activities. • Any other related duties as assigned Required Skills & Experience: • Minimum 5 years of approximately related experience required. Apply Now First Name (required) dec8478b Last Name (required) 27809534 Email (required) ad0506ad Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert b2c6caee Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Admissions & Recruitment Admissions & Recruitment Locations Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) b5148d0a Last Name (required) 34b555c7 Email (required) 7dc4743d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Associate Director, University Advisement- A00515 The Associate Director of University Advisement is responsible for being highly accessible, integrating services and programs in academic advising, student intervention and support, professional integrations for student development, academic integrations for student development, and social integration for student development. The Associate Director supervises a team of staff that will also provide these services in a detailed and tailored approach, positing mentorship as a key relationship dynamic and providing an intentional standard of care. These services and programs will support student success, self-efficacy, and a transformational college experience, maximizing the student-centered approach and deepening connection to the Mercy University community through all years of enrollment matriculation. Admissions Counselor- P00187 Mercy University seeks a dynamic and energetic individual to join our team on the Dobbs Ferry Campus as an Admissions Counselor with primary responsibility recruiting Westchester County. The Admissions Counselor will develop partnerships with high school counselors and corporate/community organizations while generating inquiries from prospective students that convert to enrolled students. The Admissions counselor will provide best-in-class customer service to students who have expressed an interest in attending Mercy College. The admissions counselor will use all available technology (phone, email, text, chat, etc.) to engage students immediately upon inquiry and cultivate a relationship through support and excitement for the journey ahead. Admissions counselor is often the point of contact a student has with Mercy university, to that end, we seek an enthusiastic and driven “people person” to join our team. Open Rank Professor and Clinical Director, Counseling (F00268) The School of Social and Behavioral Sciences at Mercy University invites applications for a full-time, Open Rank Professor/Clinical Director of Counseling 12-month multi-year contract position in the Department of Counseling, overseeing field experience for the School Counseling and Mental Health Counseling programs. This is an in-person position with opportunities to teach select courses online. The successful candidate will demonstrate excellence in teaching, commitment to diversity and social justice, and the ability to contribute meaningfully to graduate counseling education. About Mercy Mercy University is a dynamic, independent, coeducational New York City area university that offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate degree and certificate programs in six schools: Business, Education, Health and Natural Sciences, Liberal Arts, Nursing, and Social and Behavioral Sciences. Mercy is the region's largest private, nonprofit, Minority-Serving Institution, proud to serve a student body that is highly diverse. As a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI), Mercy University, has been ranked nationally among top colleges in the country for Hispanics by the Hispanic Association of Colleges and Universities (HACU) and by Excelencia in Education, earning their prestigious Seal of Excelencia for intentionally serving Latino students. Mercy University was further recognized by HACU as a national leader in awarding bachelor's degrees to Hispanics in several disciplines, including Psychology, Sociology, and Business. Westchester Magazine has also named Mercy the Best College in Westchester County in 2019, 2020, and 2022. Mercy is committed to offering an inclusive learning environment to help a diverse student body set a course for their future. To support its student body, Mercy has been awarded a number of federal grants which enable us to better develop and deliver education to our students. Mercy’s student body reflects the rich diversity of the New York metropolitan area. Enrollment, including full-time and part-time undergraduates and graduates, is approximately 8,800. Mercy students learn on campuses in Dobbs Ferry, the Bronx, and Manhattan as well as online. At Mercy University we strive to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. Our Mission: Mercy University is committed to providing motivated students the opportunity to transform their lives through higher education by offering liberal arts and professional programs in personalized and high-quality learning environments, thus preparing students to embark on rewarding careers, to continue learning throughout their lives and to act ethically and responsibly in a changing world. Benefits Eligible: Mercy University strives to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. EEO Statement Mercy University is an equal opportunity employer. Mercy University actively engages in recruiting a diverse workforce and student body that includes members of historically underrepresented groups and strives to build and sustain a welcoming and supportive campus community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, pregnancy, height, weight, genetic information, disability, or protected veteran status. As part of this commitment, Mercy University will ensure that persons with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations for the hiring process. If reasonable accommodation is needed, please contact The Office of Human Resources at (914) 674-7839, Option 6 or via email at HR@mercy.edu. The posted salary range for this position is based on several legitimate, non-discriminatory factors set by the organization. Mercy is committed to ensuring equal pay opportunities for equal work regardless of gender, race, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local pay equity laws. Campus Safety Mercy University is committed to providing a safe and welcoming environment for all. Information regarding campus safety can be found here . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
