      "description": "Admissions Counselor- P00187 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Admissions Counselor- P00187 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Admissions Counselor- P00187 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Full-time $55,000 annually Add to favorites View favorites Mercy University seeks a dynamic and energetic individual to join our team on the Dobbs Ferry Campus as an Admissions Counselor with primary responsibility recruiting Westchester County. The Admissions Counselor will develop partnerships with high school counselors and corporate/community organizations while generating inquiries from prospective students that convert to enrolled students. The Admissions counselor will provide best-in-class customer service to students who have expressed an interest in attending Mercy College. The admissions counselor will use all available technology (phone, email, text, chat, etc.) to engage students immediately upon inquiry and cultivate a relationship through support and excitement for the journey ahead. Admissions counselor is often the point of contact a student has with Mercy university, to that end, we seek an enthusiastic and driven “people person” to join our team. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: • Recruitment: Represent Mercy University at recruitment events, college fairs, high schools, and community outreach programs to attract potential students and promote the institution's academic offerings and benefits. • Student Relations management o Provide guidance, recommendations, and information to interested students. o Promote next steps in recruitment process (campus visitation, applying, etc.) o Set up appointments for Admission Counselors and campus visitation. o Use the CRM system to record all student communications. o Provide insight on how processes might be adjusted to improve customer experience. o Assist in the inputting of electronic and paper-based inquiry forms o Ability to work evenings and weekends. • Event Planning: Assist in planning and executing admission-related events, such as open houses, admitted student days, and orientation programs. Required Skills & Experience: • Demonstrates strong communication skills, both oral and written • Comfortable engaging and connecting with prospective students both in person and on the phone. • Experience giving presentations to prospective students, their families, advisors, counselors, and others in partnership organizations. • Motivated, with a sense of urgency to achieve individual, team, departmental, and University goals. • Exhibits tenacity and creativity in addressing and solving problems. • Team player who is just as excited to work collaboratively as autonomously. • Proficient in MS Office and Outlook, Banner, Slate, and other software relevant and necessary to perform in an admission office. • Ability to travel locally daily and work occasional nights and Saturdays. Education Requirements: • Bachelor's degree Physical/Other Requirements: • Must have a valid driver’s license and a car. • Must be able to push, pull, move, or lift to 50 lbs. • Must be able to meet all general health requirements for the position as per college policies. Apply Now First Name (required) 35ba59d9 Last Name (required) 096b2816 Email (required) b524b97e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert a7437613 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Admissions & Recruitment Admissions & Recruitment Locations Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 12bc4c14 Last Name (required) 97ce9936 Email (required) f1cf27bf Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Associate Director, University Advisement- 