    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/undergraduate-associate-dean-school-of-nursing-f00622-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing (F00622)",
      "description": "Undergraduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing (F00622) - New York, United States Undergraduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing (F00622) - New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Undergraduate Associate Dean, School of Nursing (F00622) New York, United States Faculty Full-time $115,000 - $160,000 Add to favorites View favorites Job Summary: The Undergraduate Associate Dean for the School of Nursing provides operational and academic leadership to support the school’s mission of excellence in nursing education. Reporting directly to the Senior Associate Dean/ Chief Nursing Officer, the Associate Dean is responsible for assisting in the oversight and development of the undergraduate nursing faculty, setting course schedules, participating in nursing governance, contributing to curriculum and policy review and revision, teaching in courses based upon expertise, and assisting in ensuring the programs meet state regulatory and national accreditation standards. Reporting directly to the Senior Associate Dean, the Associate Dean works collaboratively with faculty, staff, and administrators to advance the Nursing Programs' mission. KEY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES: Leadership Fosters a positive work environment grounded in strong communication and collaboration within the department. Establishes program and department-related goals and initiatives that support the overall mission of the school and university. Provides guidance to program directors (PDs) to ensure academic integrity and teaching excellence within programs. Addresses faculty and student matters within programs and the department in alignment with university and school policies Maintains teaching and service responsibilities aligned with area of expertise Administration & Operations Oversee daily operations of Undergraduate Nursing Programs. Assist in budget preparation, resource allocation, and strategic planning. Curriculum Assist in the design, development, evaluation, and continuous improvement of nursing curricula to ensure alignment with accreditation standards, licensure requirements, and emerging trends in healthcare education. Collaborate with faculty and program directors to integrate evidence-based practice, health equity, technology, and innovation across all academic programs. Assist in leading curriculum review processes, including course mapping, assessment planning, and outcome evaluation to support academic rigor and student success. Oversee the implementation of academic policies and procedures related to curriculum, progression, grading, and program integrity within the UG program. Accreditation Work with nursing leadership and faculty to ensure compliance with regulatory agencies, licensing bodies, and accreditation requirements. Assist in the preparation of reports, self-studies, and documentation for program review and accreditation visits. Monitor evolving accreditation standards. Assessment Management of the comprehensive evaluation plan for all nursing academic programs, ensuring alignment with AACN Essentials (2021). Oversee the School’s ongoing assessment process for undergraduate programs, including timely submission of required reports. Work with Program Directors and assessment coordinator(s) to ensure syllabi clearly articulate student learning and professional development outcomes Ensure that student learning outcomes are achieved and measurable through both qualitative and quantitative methods. Promote data-informed assessment of student academic achievement and retention. Collaborate with the School Assessment Committee and assist programs preparing for university-based program reviews. Partner with the Dean and Sr. Associate Dean to implement and evaluate the school’s institutional effectiveness plan. Assist the CNO with timely preparation and submission of reports related to curriculum for internal governance, accreditation bodies, and regulatory agencies. Teaching Teach a minimum of 12 credits annually to remain actively engaged in teaching excellence, maintain familiarity with learning management system, and understand evolving instructional practices and student needs. Other Responsibilities: Serve on a twelve-month contract. Perform additional duties as assigned Education and Experience Requirements: Earned doctorate in nursing or related field (DNP, EdD, or PhD), at least one graduate degree must be in nursing Minimum of seven years of teaching experience at postsecondary level. Rank of Associate or Professor required. Five years of progressive administrative experience Skills and Competencies: Applicants must have knowledge of the structure and organization of health and education systems Demonstrate capacity to manage multiple projects, set priorities, and coordinate efforts within and across academic units Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to organize and present information clearly and analytically in both face-to-face and virtual environments Strong communicator with the ability to engage faculty, staff, students, and academic leaders Demonstrated interpersonal and collaborative skills in working with faculty, students, staff, and external stakeholders Commitment to fostering a positive, team-oriented environment that reflects respect, equity, and professional integrity Physical/Other Requirements: Must be able to perform tasks that may involve pushing, pulling, moving, or lifting up to 50 lbs., with reasonable accommodations as needed Must meet all role-specific general health and safety requirements in accordance with university policies and guidelines upon hire, with reasonable accommodations provided as needed. Application Instructions: Cover letter describing the applicant's experience related to the required qualifications CV, including publications and grants Names and contact information for three references. Apply Now First Name (required) ed16b1d9 Last Name (required) 8cdba665 Email (required) 4aade270 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 4f68abe0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Nursing School of Nursing Locations New York, United States New York, United States First Name (required) e8f8dc30 Last Name (required) 79f220db Email (required) 714b3f53 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Associate Director, University Advisement- A00515 The Associate Director of University Advisement is responsible for being highly accessible, integrating services and programs in academic advising, student intervention and support, professional integrations for student development, academic integrations for student development, and social integration for student development. The Associate Director supervises a team of staff that will also provide these services in a detailed and tailored approach, positing mentorship as a key relationship dynamic and providing an intentional standard of care. These services and programs will support student success, self-efficacy, and a transformational college experience, maximizing the student-centered approach and deepening connection to the Mercy University community through all years of enrollment matriculation. Admissions Counselor- P00187 Mercy University seeks a dynamic and energetic individual to join our team on the Dobbs Ferry Campus as an Admissions Counselor with primary responsibility recruiting Westchester County. The Admissions Counselor will develop partnerships with high school counselors and corporate/community organizations while generating inquiries from prospective students that convert to enrolled students. The Admissions counselor will provide best-in-class customer service to students who have expressed an interest in attending Mercy College. The admissions counselor will use all available technology (phone, email, text, chat, etc.) to engage students immediately upon inquiry and cultivate a relationship through support and excitement for the journey ahead. Admissions counselor is often the point of contact a student has with Mercy university, to that end, we seek an enthusiastic and driven “people person” to join our team. Open Rank Professor and Clinical Director, Counseling (F00268) The School of Social and Behavioral Sciences at Mercy University invites applications for a full-time, Open Rank Professor/Clinical Director of Counseling 12-month multi-year contract position in the Department of Counseling, overseeing field experience for the School Counseling and Mental Health Counseling programs. This is an in-person position with opportunities to teach select courses online. The successful candidate will demonstrate excellence in teaching, commitment to diversity and social justice, and the ability to contribute meaningfully to graduate counseling education. About Mercy Mercy University is a dynamic, independent, coeducational New York City area university that offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate degree and certificate programs in six schools: Business, Education, Health and Natural Sciences, Liberal Arts, Nursing, and Social and Behavioral Sciences. Mercy is the region's largest private, nonprofit, Minority-Serving Institution, proud to serve a student body that is highly diverse. As a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI), Mercy University, has been ranked nationally among top colleges in the country for Hispanics by the Hispanic Association of Colleges and Universities (HACU) and by Excelencia in Education, earning their prestigious Seal of Excelencia for intentionally serving Latino students. Mercy University was further recognized by HACU as a national leader in awarding bachelor's degrees to Hispanics in several disciplines, including Psychology, Sociology, and Business. Westchester Magazine has also named Mercy the Best College in Westchester County in 2019, 2020, and 2022. Mercy is committed to offering an inclusive learning environment to help a diverse student body set a course for their future. To support its student body, Mercy has been awarded a number of federal grants which enable us to better develop and deliver education to our students. Mercy’s student body reflects the rich diversity of the New York metropolitan area. Enrollment, including full-time and part-time undergraduates and graduates, is approximately 8,800. Mercy students learn on campuses in Dobbs Ferry, the Bronx, and Manhattan as well as online. At Mercy University we strive to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. Our Mission: Mercy University is committed to providing motivated students the opportunity to transform their lives through higher education by offering liberal arts and professional programs in personalized and high-quality learning environments, thus preparing students to embark on rewarding careers, to continue learning throughout their lives and to act ethically and responsibly in a changing world. Benefits Eligible: Mercy University strives to provide employees and their families with a comprehensive and valuable benefits package. We offer high-quality health care plans, retirement benefits, tuition discounts, flexible spending, and much more. EEO Statement Mercy University is an equal opportunity employer. Mercy University actively engages in recruiting a diverse workforce and student body that includes members of historically underrepresented groups and strives to build and sustain a welcoming and supportive campus community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, creed, religion, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, pregnancy, height, weight, genetic information, disability, or protected veteran status. As part of this commitment, Mercy University will ensure that persons with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations for the hiring process. If reasonable accommodation is needed, please contact The Office of Human Resources at (914) 674-7839, Option 6 or via email at HR@mercy.edu. The posted salary range for this position is based on several legitimate, non-discriminatory factors set by the organization. Mercy is committed to ensuring equal pay opportunities for equal work regardless of gender, race, or any other category protected by federal, state, or local pay equity laws. Campus Safety Mercy University is committed to providing a safe and welcoming environment for all. Information regarding campus safety can be found here . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
