    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-early-childhood-and-childhood-education-f00632-dobbs-ferry-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Early Childhood and Childhood Education (F00632)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Early Childhood and Childhood Education (F00632) - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Assistant Professor, Early Childhood and Childhood Education (F00632) - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Assistant Professor, Early Childhood and Childhood Education (F00632) Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Faculty Full-time $70,000 – $75,000 (commensurate with experience and qualifications) Add to favorites View favorites Position Description: The Department of Early Childhood and Childhood Education at Mercy University invites applications for an Assistant Professor position to start September 1, 2027. We are seeking a highly organized, student-centered Assistant Professor to support the launch and ongoing implementation of the Suzanne McGraw Scholars Program, an exclusive pathway preparing future educators who will teach at the early childhood education level. This faculty position focuses on academic leadership of the program. Some evenings and weekends may be required. Primary Responsibilities: Teaching: • Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in early childhood and/or childhood education, including instructional methods, foundations, and curriculum design • Advise and mentor students across stages of the teacher preparation process • Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, and departmental initiatives • Maintain a commitment to culturally responsive, inclusive, and evidence-based instruction Required Qualifications: • Earned doctorate in Early Childhood Education, Childhood Education, Curriculum & Instruction, or a closely related field • Demonstrated leadership, organizational, and communication skills • Familiarity with teacher certification standards and state education requirements, particularly in New York • Commitment to equity, access, and culturally responsive education Preferred Qualifications: • Experience teaching in higher education • Minimum of three years of teaching experience in P–6 settings, some of which specifically includes pre-K experience • Knowledge of accreditation processes (e.g., CAEP) and assessment practices • Familiarity with special education as well as early childhood/childhood education Apply Now First Name (required) d3721181 Last Name (required) 820d0e9d Email (required) e564f5b9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 62b05f6c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Education School of Education Locations Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 39e59bfc Last Name (required) 28c58442 Email (required) 63c29545 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Associate Director, University Advisement- A00515 The Associate Director of University Advisement is responsible for being highly accessible, integrating services and programs in academic advising, student intervention and support, professional integrations for student development, academic integrations for student development, and social integration for student development. The Associate Director supervises a team of staff that will also provide these services in a detailed and tailored approach, positing mentorship as a key relationship dynamic and providing an intentional standard of care. These services and programs will support student success, self-efficacy, and a transformational college experience, maximizing the student-centered approach and deepening connection to the Mercy University community through all years of enrollment matriculation. Admissions Counselor- P00187 Mercy University seeks a dynamic and energetic individual to join our team on the Dobbs Ferry Campus as an Admissions Counselor with pr