    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/registrar-a00067-dobbs-ferry-ny-new-york-united-states": {
      "title": "Registrar- A00067",
      "description": "Registrar- A00067 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Registrar- A00067 - Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Kiosk mode So Take the Next Steps Registrar- A00067 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Full-time $140,000- $175,000 annually Add to favorites View favorites JOB SUMMARY The Registrar will serve as the steward of student data and be responsible for managing all processes related to the student life cycle, from enrollment to degree completion. This position will also ensure that all regulatory reporting requirements are submitted on a timely basis. The Registrar will report directly to the Associate Vice President of Data Analysis, AI and Strategy, and Executive Director of Financial Planning and Academic Operations within the Office of the Provost. The ideal candidate will be able to leverage technology to improve registrar processes in order to enhance the student experience and promote student success. This individual will also demonstrate key team-building qualities and be able to provide training and guidance to junior team members. Direct reports to the Registrar include: • Deputy University Registrar • Associate Registrar for Commencement & Curriculum • Associate University Registrar for Data Analysis and Reporting The 3 direct reports are currently supported by: • Assistant University Registrar for Strategic Scheduling, Calendaring & Curriculum • Assistant University Registrar for Conferral, Commencement & Compliance • Assistant University Registrar for Records, Registration & Processing • Registrar Scheduling Specialists • Student Record Specialists ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS & RESPONSIBILITIES Regulatory Compliance, Records & Reporting Review and strengthen data gathering and reporting systems Lead necessary change management to make systems more efficient and functional Interpretation and enforcement of current federal regulations related to student records management and regulatory reporting requirements Regulatory reporting to Student Clearinghouse, New York State and Federal agencies Provide FERPA training to all employees with access to student records Maintain the University’s student records, including archived student records, in all formats according to industry standards and the requirements of accreditation agencies Oversight of the preparation and dissemination of student Dismissal, Probation, and Dean’s List data Office Leadership, Operations & Staff Development Hiring, training, mentoring, and assessment of Registrar Office staff Development of Standard Operating Procedures and calendar for Registrar Office processes Lead assessment and effectiveness of the organizational structure on a regular basis Lead professional development activities and represent the University to outside organizations Academic Operations, Scheduling & Graduation Participate on academic committees such as Undergraduate Curriculum Committee, Graduate Curriculum Committee, etc. In coordination with the Office of Academic Affairs, set up procedures to ensure the college’s academic policies are complied with consistently, including classroom scheduling, degree audit, graduation, transfer credit entry, transcript processing, record-keeping, and related reporting including revisions of polices as necessary Ensure the academic course schedules meet the demands of Mercy’s students while balancing fiscal resources Lead academic administrators in the development and publication of semester course schedules Oversee the preparation of the Academic Calendar and Catalogs Lead all Registrar Office Commencement activities that include managing degree conferrals, providing honors designations, commencement and program preparation Other duties related to the functions of the Registrar’s Office, as well as additional responsibilities assigned by the supervisor Technology, Data & Institutional Collaboration Effectively utilize Ellucian Banner to manage, maintain, and access information accurately and efficiently in support of operations, processes, and institutional objectives. Lead all IT projects related to Registrar Office processes and reporting requirements Manage key elements of the University’s student information system and other software applications used to support the Office of the Provost Monitor, analyze, and report on data trends that may impact strategically on existing or future projects/processes. Work closely with other college offices, including Admissions, Enrollment Services, Academic Affairs and Technology Services, to assist in the recruitment and retention of students Lead efforts to increase and enhance automation QUALIFICATIONS The ideal candidate will be committed to the mission of Mercy University and have a passion for fostering student success and a deep understanding of the complexities of higher education. Minimum of seven to ten years of progressively responsible experience with academic records and registration, including a minimum of five years of experience in a senior leadership role, or equivalent combination of experience and education Thorough knowledge of federal and state laws and mandates related to enrollment and student records with an understanding of institutional compliance responsibilities, including FERPA Strong commitment to delivering excellent customer service to students, faculty, staff, alumni, and other constituents Strong analytical skills with the ability to collect, organize, analyze, and disseminate significant amounts of information with attention to detail and accuracy Strong management skills, including the ability to direct and motivate staff responsible for time-sensitive, customer-oriented processes Strong Communication skills, including the ability to communicate complex registrar operations at a high level to non-subject area leaders Excellent analytical, reasoning, and organizational skills and an affinity toward and with technology Proven ability to relate effectively to a wide variety of people of diverse backgrounds, including an understanding and respect for cultural, ethnic, and individual differences Expert-level proficiency with Banner is essential Prior experience with Banner, Coursedog, SLATE, DegreeWorks, Parchment/Instructure, and Tableau is a plus Ability to travel within multi-campus environment Able to work beyond normal working hours as needed. May require irregular work hours, such as evenings and/or weekends Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree preferred Apply Now First Name (required) 7122876f Last Name (required) 5803a74a Email (required) 5364e218 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert c592a92b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Registrar Registrar Locations Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States First Name (required) 2007b8f7 Last Name (required) c3afb202 Email (required) 424083c7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs: Associate Director, University Advisement- A00515 The Associate Director of University Advisement is responsible for being highly accessible, integrating services and programs in academic advising, student intervention and support, professional integrations for student development, academic integrations for student development, and social integration for student development. The Associate Director supervises a team of staff that will also provide these services in a detailed and tailored approach, positing mentorship as a key relationship dynamic and providing an intentional standard of care. These services and programs will support student success, self-efficacy, and a transformational college experience, maximizing the student-centered approach and deepening connection to the Mercy University community thr